    "body": "## Overview\n\nFixes #65693. In `/v1/messages` streaming, a tool call whose streamed arguments never became JSON because generation stopped on EOS or a stop token id now ends with `stop_reason: \"end_turn\"` instead of `\"tool_use\"`, the way a call cut by a stop string already ends with `stop_sequence`.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Streamed arguments that are not JSON when generation stops naturally give `end_turn`, whether the chat layer finished with `tool_calls` or `stop`, and with a natural EOS or a stop token id.\n- Complete calls, calls with no arguments streamed (empty or whitespace, as for a tool without parameters), `max_tokens` and stop strings map as before.\n- The non-streaming path is unchanged. The issue explains why it needs a parser change instead.\n\n## Validation\n\n```\n# the new cases against main's serving.py (75f676149)\npytest tests/entrypoints/anthropic/test_anthropic_messages_conversion.py -k TestToolUseStopReason\nE       AssertionError: assert 'tool_use' == 'end_turn'\n3 failed, 8 passed\n# this branch\npytest tests/entrypoints/anthropic/test_anthropic_messages_conversion.py\n141 passed\npytest tests/entrypoints/anthropic\n167 passed\n```\n\nThe server tests ran with `Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B` on an RTX 4070 Ti SUPER, with `VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_SAMPLER=0` because FlashInfer's sampling JIT build fails on that machine. The live behaviour this fixes is in the issue: Qwen3.8-27B-FP8 on vLLM 0.32.0 finishing a stream with `tool_calls` and unterminated arguments when a stop token id falls inside them, and a Claude Code session whose call stopped on EOS.\n\n## Details\n\n`tool_cut` is passed only by the stream converter, where the streamed arguments are known. It is true when arguments were streamed and do not parse, which is when `tool_complete` is false for a reason other than a call without parameters. #60621 changes `_is_json` to treat empty or whitespace arguments as complete. This change leaves those calls alone, so the two compose.\n\nNot a duplicate: #60621 covers calls with no arguments, #42213 covers a Chat Completions stream that stops before any tool delta, and #57707 and #59882 change how the qwen3 converter closes a parameter. None of them changes the stop reason of a call cut inside its arguments.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
